module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjLocalizedRingMap
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.VeryAmpleAffineBase.AwayFraction

/-!
# The generators of a cutting chart, read in a coordinate chart

The coordinate cut of [Stacks, Tag 02NP] covers `X` by the charts `α⁻¹(D₊(g_j))` of standard
opens of homogeneous elements `g_j` of positive degree `d_j`, on which `α` is a closed immersion,
and writes the algebra generators of each over the base as fractions `b / g_j^k`
(`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_finset_away_forall_mem_closure`). It then has to see those
generators in a *coordinate* chart `D₊(y_i)` of a degree-one `y_i`, where the morphism to `ℙⁿ_S`
is pinned. Whenever `D₊(g) ⊆ D₊(y_i)` the passage is

  `b / g^k = (b / y_i^{k·dg}) · (g / y_i^{dg})^{-k}`,

and this file proves it, together with its consequence: the generator is a polynomial over `𝒜 0`
in the coordinate ratios `y_m / y_i` and the inverse of `g / y_i^{dg}`.

## The containment `D₊(g) ⊆ D₊(y_i)` costs nothing

It is not a restriction on the source's cover. `D₊(y_i g_j) = D₊(y_i) ⊓ D₊(g_j)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen_mul`), and `y_i g_j` is again homogeneous of positive degree
`1 + d_j`, so the overlap of a coordinate chart with a cutting chart is itself a standard open of
the same kind: it lies in `α.coborderRange` because `D₊(g_j)` does
(`ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen_mul_le_right`), hence its chart is affine, `α` restricts to a
closed immersion over it, and its sections are fractions — all by
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isAffineOpen_preimage_basicOpen`,
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.isClosedImmersion_restrict_basicOpen` and
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.surjective_awayToChart` applied at `y_i g_j`. So the cut may be taken
with `g := y_i g_j` from the start, and then `D₊(g) ⊆ D₊(y_i)` holds by
`ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen_mul_le_left`.

## The comparison of the two charts is already available

The restriction maps of `Proj` between standard opens — the comparison of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 g` with `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 y_i` — are
already in the library: `ProjectiveSpectrum.degreeZeroRingMap` is the map `A₍f₎ ⟶ A₍h₎` attached to
`D₊(h) ⊆ D₊(f)`, `ProjectiveSpectrum.awayToSection_degreeZeroRingMap` identifies it with the
restriction map of the structure sheaf of `Proj`, and
`ProjectiveSpectrum.isLocalizationAway_degreeZeroRingMap` says that `A₍h₎` is the localization of
`A₍f₎` at `h^{deg f} / f^{deg h}` — which for `f = y_i` of degree one is exactly the
`h / y_i^{deg h}` this file inverts, so an inverse `w` always exists. So nothing about the
comparison is rebuilt here; what is added is the *arithmetic* of the three fractions under it.

## How the identity is proved

`ProjectiveSpectrum.val_degreeZeroRingMap` turns the restriction into the canonical `A`-algebra
map of ordinary localizations, so all three fractions can be compared in `Localization.Away g`.
There the only facts used are that an `A`-algebra map out of `A_f` sends `x / f^n` to something
whose product with the `n`-th power of the image of `f` is the image of `x`
(`Stacks.OverlapFraction.algHom_mk_mul_pow`), and that the image of `y_i` is a unit
(`ProjectiveSpectrum.isUnit_algebraMap_away_of_basicOpen_le`). Clearing the three denominators
reduces the claim to `b · y_i^{k·dg} = b · y_i^{k·dg}`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.OverlapFraction.localization_mk_mul_pow`,
  `Stacks.OverlapFraction.algHom_mk_mul_pow`,
  `Stacks.OverlapFraction.val_degreeZeroRingMap_mk_mul_pow`: clearing a denominator, in the
  localization, along an `A`-algebra map out of it, and along a restriction map of degree-zero
  localizations.
* `Stacks.OverlapFraction.restrictCoord`: the restriction `A₍q₎ ⟶ A₍g₎` for `q` of degree one and
  `D₊(g) ⊆ D₊(q)`.
* `Stacks.OverlapFraction.restrictCoord_mk_mul_mk_eq_one`: `g/q^{dg}` is invertible in `A₍g₎`,
  with inverse `q^{dg}/g`.
* `Stacks.OverlapFraction.mk_mul_restrictCoord_pow`: **the identity**, in the inverse-free form
  `(b/g^k)·(g/q^{dg})^k = b/q^{k·dg}` in `A₍g₎`.
* `Stacks.OverlapFraction.mk_mem_closure` and
  `Stacks.OverlapFraction.mk_mem_closure_mk`: **the surjectivity input of the coordinate cut** —
  the generator `b/g^k` lies in the subring generated by the degree-zero constants, the
  restricted ratios `y_m/y_i`, and an inverse of `g/y_i^{dg}`; the second form exhibits that
  inverse as `y_i^{dg}/g` and so carries no hypothesis beyond the choice data.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open HomogeneousLocalization

universe u w

namespace Stacks.OverlapFraction

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜]

/-! ### Clearing a denominator -/

/-- **`(x / f^n) · f^n = x` in `A_f`.** -/
theorem localization_mk_mul_pow (f x : A) (n : ℕ) (hn : f ^ n ∈ Submonoid.powers f) :
    Localization.mk x ⟨f ^ n, hn⟩ * algebraMap A (Localization.Away f) f ^ n =
      algebraMap A (Localization.Away f) x := by
  rw [← map_pow, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap,
    Localization.mk_mul, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
  exact ⟨1, by simp; ring⟩

/-- **Clearing the denominator along an `A`-algebra map out of `A_f`**: the image of `x / f^n`
times the `n`-th power of the image of `f` is the image of `x`. -/
theorem algHom_mk_mul_pow {T : Type*} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] (f : A)
    (ψ : Localization.Away f →ₐ[A] T) (x : A) (n : ℕ) (hn : f ^ n ∈ Submonoid.powers f) :
    ψ (Localization.mk x ⟨f ^ n, hn⟩) * algebraMap A T f ^ n = algebraMap A T x :=
  calc ψ (Localization.mk x ⟨f ^ n, hn⟩) * algebraMap A T f ^ n
      = ψ (Localization.mk x ⟨f ^ n, hn⟩ * algebraMap A (Localization.Away f) f ^ n) := by
        rw [map_mul, map_pow, ψ.commutes]
    _ = algebraMap A T x := by rw [localization_mk_mul_pow, ψ.commutes]

/-- **Clearing the denominator of a fraction along a restriction map of degree-zero
localizations.** -/
theorem val_degreeZeroRingMap_mk_mul_pow (f h : A)
    (hf : ∃ e : ℕ, 0 < e ∧ f ∈ 𝒜 e) (hh : ∃ e : ℕ, 0 < e ∧ h ∈ 𝒜 e)
    (hfh : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 h ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 f)
    {e n : ℕ} (hfe : f ∈ 𝒜 e) (x : A) (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 (n • e)) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.val
        (ProjectiveSpectrum.degreeZeroRingMap 𝒜 f h hf hh hfh (Away.mk 𝒜 hfe n x hx)) *
          algebraMap A (Localization.Away h) f ^ n =
      algebraMap A (Localization.Away h) x := by
  rw [ProjectiveSpectrum.val_degreeZeroRingMap, Away.val_mk]
  exact algHom_mk_mul_pow f (ProjectiveSpectrum.localizedRingMap 𝒜 f h hf hh hfh) x n _

/-! ### The restriction into a coordinate chart -/

section Restrict

variable {dg : ℕ} {q g : A}

/-- **Restriction from the coordinate chart to a standard open inside it**, `A₍q₎ ⟶ A₍g₎`, for
`q` homogeneous of degree one and `D₊(g) ⊆ D₊(q)`. -/
abbrev restrictCoord (hq : q ∈ 𝒜 1) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg) (hdg : 0 < dg)
    (hgq : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 q) :
    Away 𝒜 q →ₐ[𝒜 0] Away 𝒜 g :=
  ProjectiveSpectrum.degreeZeroRingMap 𝒜 q g ⟨1, Nat.one_pos, hq⟩ ⟨dg, hdg, hg⟩ hgq

/-- Clearing the denominator of `x / g^k` in `A₍g₎`, read in `A_g`. -/
private theorem val_away_mk_mul_pow {g : A} {dg : ℕ} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg) (k : ℕ) {x : A}
    (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 (k * dg)) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.val (Away.mk 𝒜 hg k x (by simpa using hx)) *
        algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) g ^ k = algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) x := by
  rw [Away.val_mk]
  exact localization_mk_mul_pow g x k _

/-- Clearing the denominator of the restricted `g / q^{dg}` in `A_g`. -/
private theorem val_restrictCoord_mk_mul_pow (hq : q ∈ 𝒜 1) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg) (hdg : 0 < dg)
    (hgq : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 q) :
    HomogeneousLocalization.val
      (restrictCoord 𝒜 hq hg hdg hgq (Away.mk 𝒜 hq dg g (by simpa using hg))) *
        algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) q ^ dg = algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) g :=
  val_degreeZeroRingMap_mk_mul_pow 𝒜 q g _ _ hgq hq g _

/-- **The fraction `g / q^{dg}` is invertible in `A₍g₎`, with inverse `q^{dg} / g`.** This is the
one fact that makes the passage of `Stacks.OverlapFraction.mk_mul_restrictCoord_pow` into a
division. It is also the content of
`ProjectiveSpectrum.isLocalizationAway_degreeZeroRingMap`, which says that `A₍g₎` is `A₍q₎`
localized at this very fraction; the inverse is exhibited directly here instead, so that no
localization instance has to be transported. -/
theorem restrictCoord_mk_mul_mk_eq_one (hq : q ∈ 𝒜 1) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg) (hdg : 0 < dg)
    (hgq : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 q) :
    restrictCoord 𝒜 hq hg hdg hgq (Away.mk 𝒜 hq dg g (by simpa using hg)) *
        Away.mk 𝒜 hg 1 (q ^ dg) (by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded dg hq) = 1 := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective (Submonoid.powers g)
  have hu := val_restrictCoord_mk_mul_pow 𝒜 hq hg hdg hgq
  have hw := val_away_mk_mul_pow 𝒜 hg 1
    (x := q ^ dg) (by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded dg hq)
  rw [pow_one, map_pow] at hw
  refine (((ProjectiveSpectrum.isUnit_algebraMap_away_of_basicOpen_le 𝒜 hq Nat.one_pos hg hdg
    hgq).pow dg).mul (IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit
      (S := Localization.Away g) g)).mul_left_inj.mp ?_
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, HomogeneousLocalization.val_one, one_mul]
  linear_combination
    (HomogeneousLocalization.val
      (Away.mk 𝒜 hg 1 (q ^ dg) (by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded dg hq)) *
      algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) g) * hu +
    algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) g * hw

/-- **The identity the coordinate cut of [Stacks, Tag 02NP] needs**: in `A₍g₎` the fraction
`b / g^k` is `b / q^{k·dg}` divided by `(g / q^{dg})^k`, stated without any inverse —

  `(b/g^k) · ((g/q^{dg})|_{D₊(g)})^k = (b/q^{k·dg})|_{D₊(g)}`.

Both sides are compared in the ordinary localization `A_g`, where the restriction is the
canonical `A`-algebra map (`ProjectiveSpectrum.val_degreeZeroRingMap`); clearing the three
denominators turns the claim into `b · q^{k·dg} = b · q^{k·dg}`, and the image of `q` is a unit
by `ProjectiveSpectrum.isUnit_algebraMap_away_of_basicOpen_le`. -/
theorem mk_mul_restrictCoord_pow (hq : q ∈ 𝒜 1) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg) (hdg : 0 < dg)
    (hgq : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 q) (k : ℕ)
    {b : A} (hb : b ∈ 𝒜 (k * dg)) :
    Away.mk 𝒜 hg k b (by simpa using hb) *
        restrictCoord 𝒜 hq hg hdg hgq (Away.mk 𝒜 hq dg g (by simpa using hg)) ^ k =
      restrictCoord 𝒜 hq hg hdg hgq (Away.mk 𝒜 hq (k * dg) b (by simpa using hb)) := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective (Submonoid.powers g)
  have hz := val_away_mk_mul_pow 𝒜 hg k hb
  have hu := val_restrictCoord_mk_mul_pow 𝒜 hq hg hdg hgq
  have hv := val_degreeZeroRingMap_mk_mul_pow 𝒜 q g (hf := ⟨1, Nat.one_pos, hq⟩)
    (hh := ⟨dg, hdg, hg⟩) hgq hq b (by simpa using hb)
  refine ((ProjectiveSpectrum.isUnit_algebraMap_away_of_basicOpen_le 𝒜 hq Nat.one_pos hg hdg
    hgq).pow (k * dg)).mul_left_inj.mp ?_
  rw [hv, HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, HomogeneousLocalization.val_pow, ← hz, ← hu,
    mul_pow, ← pow_mul, Nat.mul_comm dg k]
  ring

end Restrict

/-! ### The generators of the cutting chart, in the coordinate chart -/

section Generators

variable {ι : Type*} {dg : ℕ} {g : A}

/-- **The surjectivity input of the coordinate cut of [Stacks, Tag 02NP].** Let `y : ι → A` be a
family of elements of `𝒜 1`, let `g` be homogeneous of positive degree `dg` with
`D₊(g) ⊆ D₊(y_i)`, and let `b` be homogeneous of degree `k · dg` and lie in the subalgebra
generated over `𝒜 0` by the family. Let `w` be an inverse in `A₍g₎` of the degree-zero fraction
`g / y_i^{dg}`. Then the chart generator `b / g^k` lies in the subring generated by the
degree-zero constants, the restricted coordinate ratios `y_m / y_i`, and `w`.

The ratios are what the section-value dictionary of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/VeryAmpleAffineBase/SectionDictionary.lean` converts into the
coordinate ratios `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.ratio` of the pinned family, the constants are
the base sections, and `w` is the inverse of `F_j / T_i^{dg}` on the basic open of `D₊(T_i)` in
`ℙⁿ_S` cut out by it; an inverse exists by
`ProjectiveSpectrum.isLocalizationAway_degreeZeroRingMap`.

The two ingredients are `Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_mem_closure_of_mem_adjoin`, which writes
`b / y_i^{k·dg}` as a polynomial over `𝒜 0` in the ratios, and
`Stacks.OverlapFraction.mk_mul_restrictCoord_pow`, which says that `b / g^k` is that fraction
divided by `(g / y_i^{dg})^k`. -/
theorem mk_mem_closure (y : ι → A) (hy : ∀ j, y j ∈ 𝒜 1) (i : ι) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg) (hdg : 0 < dg)
    (hgq : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 (y i))
    {k : ℕ} {b : A} (hb : b ∈ 𝒜 (k * dg))
    (hbmem : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range y)) {w : Away 𝒜 g}
    (hw : restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq
      (Away.mk 𝒜 (hy i) dg g (by simpa using hg)) * w = 1) :
    Away.mk 𝒜 hg k b (by simpa using hb) ∈
      Subring.closure (Set.range (algebraMap (𝒜 0) (Away 𝒜 g)) ∪
        Set.range (fun m : ι => restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq
          (Away.mk 𝒜 (hy i) 1 (y m) (by simpa using hy m))) ∪ {w}) := by
  classical
  -- The generator is the coordinate fraction divided by `(g / y_i^{dg})^k`.
  have hzw : Away.mk 𝒜 hg k b (by simpa using hb) =
      restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq (Away.mk 𝒜 (hy i) (k * dg) b (by simpa using hb)) *
        w ^ k := by
    rw [← mk_mul_restrictCoord_pow 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq k hb, mul_assoc, ← mul_pow, hw, one_pow,
      mul_one]
  rw [hzw]
  set T : Set (Away 𝒜 g) :=
    Set.range (algebraMap (𝒜 0) (Away 𝒜 g)) ∪
      Set.range (fun m : ι => restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq
        (Away.mk 𝒜 (hy i) 1 (y m) (by simpa using hy m))) ∪ {w} with hT
  set s : Set (Away 𝒜 (y i)) :=
    Set.range (algebraMap (𝒜 0) (Away 𝒜 (y i))) ∪
      Set.range (fun j : ι => Away.mk 𝒜 (hy i) 1 (y j) (by simpa using hy j)) with hs
  refine mul_mem ?_
    (pow_mem (Subring.subset_closure (hT ▸ Set.mem_union_right _ rfl)) k)
  -- The coordinate fraction is a polynomial in the ratios, and restriction is a ring map.
  have hgen : ∀ z ∈ s, restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq z ∈ Subring.closure T := by
    rw [hs]
    rintro z (⟨r, rfl⟩ | ⟨m, rfl⟩)
    · refine Subring.subset_closure (hT ▸ Set.mem_union_left _ (Set.mem_union_left _ ⟨r, ?_⟩))
      exact ((restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq).commutes r).symm
    · exact Subring.subset_closure
        (hT ▸ Set.mem_union_left _ (Set.mem_union_right _ ⟨m, rfl⟩))
  have hle : Subring.closure s ≤
      Subring.comap (restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq).toRingHom (Subring.closure T) :=
    Subring.closure_le.mpr fun z hz => Subring.mem_comap.mpr (hgen z hz)
  exact hle (Stacks.AwayFraction.mk_mem_closure_of_mem_adjoin 𝒜 y hy i hb hbmem)

/-- **The surjectivity input of the coordinate cut of [Stacks, Tag 02NP], with the inverse
exhibited: no hypothesis beyond the choice data.** The inverse of `y_i^{dg} / g` of
`Stacks.OverlapFraction.restrictCoord_mk_mul_mk_eq_one` is substituted for the `w` of
`Stacks.OverlapFraction.mk_mem_closure`, so the generator `b / g^k` of the chart is *proved* to be
a polynomial over `𝒜 0` in the restricted coordinate ratios `y_m / y_i` together with
`y_i^{dg} / g`. -/
theorem mk_mem_closure_mk (y : ι → A) (hy : ∀ j, y j ∈ 𝒜 1) (i : ι) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 dg)
    (hdg : 0 < dg)
    (hgq : ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 (y i))
    {k : ℕ} {b : A} (hb : b ∈ 𝒜 (k * dg))
    (hbmem : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range y)) :
    Away.mk 𝒜 hg k b (by simpa using hb) ∈
      Subring.closure (Set.range (algebraMap (𝒜 0) (Away 𝒜 g)) ∪
        Set.range (fun m : ι => restrictCoord 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq
          (Away.mk 𝒜 (hy i) 1 (y m) (by simpa using hy m))) ∪
        {Away.mk 𝒜 hg 1 ((y i) ^ dg) (by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded dg (hy i))}) :=
  mk_mem_closure 𝒜 y hy i hg hdg hgq hb hbmem
    (restrictCoord_mk_mul_mk_eq_one 𝒜 (hy i) hg hdg hgq)

end Generators

end Stacks.OverlapFraction

end
